Th�otime Grohens wrote:
> Doug Freyburger wrote:
>
>> Wizards start with force bolt spell. �When I first started playing
>> wizards I wondered if that meant "force the bolt on the door to break
>> the lock" or "a bolt of force". �Whichever it means when you break down
>> a door with a spell of force bolt it counts as a successful cast and
>> counts towards enhancing the combat spell school. �Once I figured that
>> out I ended my explorations of each level early on by going around
>> closing and blasting all non-shop and non-shrine doors on each level
>> until I am offered to enhance that spell skill.
>
> In fact, just the fact of successfully casting a spell (aka not seeing
> "You fail to cast the spell correctly.") is enough to increment the
> counter for enhancing spellcasting skills, and it adds the level of
> the spell (e.g., force bolt will add 1 pt to the attack skills but
> magic missile 2).

True.  I eventually decided that practicing force bolt on doors was a
plan to deal with sleeping nymphs that might be in unexplored rooms of
the level.  If I start with blasting doors to unexplored areas I have a
better chance of seeing any nymph coming so I have  achance to take her
out with daggers.  Not a good idea to hit a nymph with force bolt in the
early game.  Blasting a wall wakes up nymphs without making it less
likely they will be able to sneak up on me.


